{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":246976,"ns":0,"title":"Square of opposition","extract":"In term logic (a branch of philosophical logic), the square of opposition is a diagram representing the relations between the four basic categorical propositions. The origin of the square can be traced back to Aristotle's tractate On Interpretation and its distinction between two oppositions: contradiction and contrariety.","description":"Type of logic diagram","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}